        {
          "path": "_m/q/q/x/f/penataran-wp/candi-panataran-main-temple-ja.jpg",
          "filename": "Candi Panataran Main Temple, Java 1299.jpg",
          "caption": "The main temple of Candi Panataran, whose west face is shown here, ascends in three large terraces\nthat bear sculptured reliefs on their walls: Ramayana on the first terrace, Krishnayana on Terrace 2, and Garudas and winged nagas on Terrace 3. Four Tantric guardians are positioned in front of the temple. The temple dates from 1347, and is thought to be the personal temple of King Hayam Wuruk, the great king of Majapahit.",
          "alt": "The main temple of Candi Panataran, whose west face is shown here, ascends in three large terraces\nthat bear sculptured reliefs on their walls: Ramayana on the first terrace, Krishnayana on Terrace 2, and Garudas and winged nagas on Terrace 3. Four Tantric guardians are positioned in front of the temple. The temple dates from 1347, and is thought to be the personal temple of King Hayam Wuruk, the great king of Majapahit.",
          "width": 3072,
          "height": 2304,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
